Duplicate / overlapping headwords in vocab.json (sweep of 2026-07-26).

Scope, the three cases as agreed:
  1. identical thai field ("A" = "A")
  2. a combined card ("A, B, C") sharing a word with another card ("B"), or two
     combined cards sharing a word ("A, B, C" and "D, C")
  3. same thing with dash-separated combined cards ("A - B" vs "B")
Comparison strips zero-width spaces. Commas and " - " inside parentheses are NOT
treated as separators, so "คำประพันธ์ (โคลง, กลอน, ฉันท์)" counts as one headword.

92 groups total. For each, write the answer on the "decision:" line. The usual
options: keep one and remove the other, keep both (real homograph or a genuinely
different sense), merge the glosses into one survivor, or trim the shared word out
of the combined card's headword.

"xref" lines mark cards that appear in more than one group, so a decision there
affects several groups at once.

Checked and dismissed, not listed below:
  chula-l4-142 "... ไป (ด้วย), ... ไป (ด้วย)" repeats itself on purpose (it is the
  shape of the grammar pattern, not two headwords).

